The code statements that lead to the bug are:
pm_runtime_put_sync(&pdev->dev);
Reason: This unconditional call decrements the runtime PM usage count. When the device is already suspended due to autosuspend (usage count 0), the decrement results in an underflow to -1, triggering the "Runtime PM usage count underflow" warning.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
pm_runtime_dont_use_autosuspend(&pdev->dev);
Reason: This function disables autosuspend without altering the usage count. It pairs correctly with `pm_runtime_use_autosuspend()` from probe, allowing `pm_runtime_disable()` to clean up the reference count properly regardless of whether the device was already suspended.

